I was just hanging out at an altar, sacrificing whatever came along to
Thoth (I was a neutral magic-user), when something occurred to me.

Artifacts can be much better for chaotic and lawful characters.  When
your god grants you a weapon from your sacrificing, the weapon will
always be co-aligned.

Chaotic characters get Stormbringer, which drains levels and does
+2 damage +8 for level drain.  It also protects againt level drains.

Lawful characters get Excalibur (+10 damage) AND Mjollnir (+24
damage!).  Excalibur protects agains level drains and helps with
searching.

What do Neutral characters get?  A few swords that add +5 to hit, but
otherwise do no extra damage, and don't even work on everything
(Giantslayer does no extra damage, and only gives "to hit" bonuses on
giants).  I'm assuming that when the spoiler file says +5, +0, it
means that it's +5 to hit, and +0 to damage.

Granted, neutral characters can (possibly) get Stormbringer by
praying, and anyone has a chance of getting Excalibur from a fountain,
and wishes will always get you what you want.

However....  There's a balance missing when two alignments can
get something REALLY good by sacrificing, and one can't.  Sacrificing
just ain't as good when you're neutral.

Sooo....

I propose that Mjollnir be made a neutral weapon.  That way, there
would be one excellent weapon for each alignment.  AD&D aside, it
would be consistent with the mythology.  While Thor (Mjollnir's owner)
certainly had lots of very lawful (& one chaotic) relatives who he was
always helping, he seemed to have a lot of neutral tendencies.


